{"requirements":[{"id":"service_management","requirement":"Manage the supplied inventory-database and inventory-api programs as services on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both supplied paths are managed by OpenRC definitions, enabled in the default runlevel, controllable through service operations, and running with live managed PIDs after a verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["prepared-dependent-workers","cmd-71cdaaef68f84cd4","cmd-6e8fd8d2bf2d425f","cmd-49b31a5015a44032","cmd-e65132a36bb6462c","cmd-bc78876285d24725"]},{"id":"readiness_ordering","requirement":"Start the API only after the database is ready.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ordered startup started the database, waited for readiness, and then started the API. During a bounded disruption, removing database readiness caused API startup to fail while remaining stopped; restarting the database restored readiness and allowed API recovery. Post-reboot observations again showed both services healthy with database-before-API start order.","evidence_ids":["cmd-86108ebc424243d6","cmd-cbb4398b9a49452b","cmd-f6435d6179f740e8","cmd-04eaf6d8e8ec4320","cmd-6e8fd8d2bf2d425f","cmd-088eeb67bd224ff8","cmd-bc78876285d24725","cmd-b688b01368bd44af"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Two hygiene issues were observed. The diagnostic invocation with --help unintentionally launched inventory-database, created a stale readiness marker, and left a process running; the process was ultimately killed and the stale state was reset during proper service startup, so this mutation was reverted. The mandatory reboot command created /tmp/mandatory-node-restart.log and left it behind, so that minor residue remained. Other mutations had clear implementation, bounded verification, recovery, or mandatory restart roles. No new listening exposure or package-health regression was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2341b7ad20664f0b","cmd-35c55fda712045bb","cmd-e7f79d58f0e54101","cmd-0f22c1953d494001","cmd-fd7e82d8e23c48f3","cmd-86108ebc424243d6","cmd-9d577040558d4c01","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The public task is satisfied. Both programs are functioning as persistent OpenRC services, and direct positive, negative, restoration, and post-reboot observations demonstrate the API readiness gate. The mandatory node-restart protocol also captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/readiness state, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe checks systemd and was unsupported on this OpenRC node, so it does not independently establish the absence of unrelated failed OpenRC services.","The supplied programs expose process and readiness-marker state and the topology contains only one node; no separate persistent application dataset or multi-node cluster state existed for an additional restart-recovery probe."]}
